# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# gas_ai/buildStamp.mjs `sourceStamp` hashes the RAW BYTES of src/, and that hash IS the
# build id the deployed app reports in Settings and that `npm run which-build` resolves
# back to commits. A CRLF checkout hashes the same source to a different id than every
# build made on CI or Linux — so a Windows-built bundle lands in its own id namespace and
# "is my fix live?" stops having an answer. Measured: LF -> bbf91fc36e4b, CRLF -> 57f7858a075e.
#
# Ten gas_ai tests also assert on source TEXT, some with hardcoded \n anchors
# (test/syncPageOverhead.test.ts slices on "spillHopPart();\n      stepIndex += 1;"), so
# they fail on a CRLF checkout and only there.
#
# core.autocrlf defaults to true on Windows; this overrides it. Every blob already in the
# object database is LF, so this changes no committed content — only what gets written out.
* text=auto eol=lf
